BT /F2 11.2 Tf 0.04 0.31 0.62 rg 50 413.5 Td (SLIDE 7 - WHAT ARE HAND LANDMARKS?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 390.5 Td (Say: A landmark is a reference point on the hand, such as a fingertip or joint. MediaPipe) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 378 Td (detects 21 landmarks for each hand. Each landmark is represented by x, y, and z) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 365.5 Td (coordinates. The numbers describe hand shape and position in a form that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 353 Td (machine-learning model can process.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 335.5 Td (Simple example: A person may look at a hand and notice a bent finger. The feature vector) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 323 Td (represents landmark positions numerically. The model learns statistical patterns from) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.3 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.20 rg 50 310.5 Td (labelled examples; it does not understand signs like a human signer.) Tj ET
